e stays within a point or breaks toward one side.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Rob Wittman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 1st District is one of the most closely watched House races of 2026, pitting six-term incumbent Rob Wittman against Henrico-area Democrat Shannon Taylor. The district leans Republican by about three points, but the midterm environment favors Democrats, and the race has drawn heavy attention because House control could hinge on it.\n\nWittman has a clear financial edge, with $4.3 million on hand to Taylor's $1.0 million, though Taylor has raised a competitive $2.1 million. A recent Democratic internal poll put the race at 47-46, and expert raters are split between Lean R and Tossup, while prediction markets give Democrats roughly a 40% chance. The race sits right on the tossup line with a modest Republican tilt.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4506, "margin": -0.72}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4359, "margin": -1.5}]}